{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-49271","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56706","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56707","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-49272","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-49274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56708","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49275","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56709","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-49276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56710","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-49277","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56711","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-56712","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-49278","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49280","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56713","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-49281","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56714","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-56715","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-49282","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56716","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-49285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56717","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-49286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56718","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49287","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56719","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-49288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56720","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56721","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-49289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56722","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49290","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56723","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-49291","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56724","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-49293","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56725","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-49295","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56726","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-49297","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56727","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-49300","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56728","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-49301","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56729","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-49304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56730","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56731","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-49305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56732","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56733","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-56734","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-56735","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56736","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-56737","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56738","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-56739","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56740","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-56741","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-49306","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56742","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49307","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56743","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-49308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56744","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56745","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-49309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56746","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49310","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56747","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-49311","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56748","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-49313","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56749","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-49315","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56750","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-49318","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56751","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-49319","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49321","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56752","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56753","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-49322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56754","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56755","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-56756","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-56757","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56758","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-56759","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-49323","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56760","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49324","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56761","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-49325","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56762","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56763","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-49326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56764","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49327","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49329","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56765","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-49328","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56766","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-49330","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56767","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-49332","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49335","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56768","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-49334","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56769","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-49336","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56770","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56771","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-49339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56772","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56773","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-56774","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-56775","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-49340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56776","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49341","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56777","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-49342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56778","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56779","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-49343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56780","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49344","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56781","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-49345","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56782","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-49348","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56783","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-49349","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56784","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-49351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56785","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-49353","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56786","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-49356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56787","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56788","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-49357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56789","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56790","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-56791","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-56792","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56793","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-56794","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-49358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56795","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49359","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56796","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-49360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56797","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56798","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-49361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56799","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49362","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56800","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-56801","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-56802","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-56803","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-56804","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-49363","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56805","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-56806","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-49366","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56807","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-49367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56808","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-49369","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56809","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-49372","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56810","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-49373","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56811","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56812","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-49376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56813","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56814","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-49377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56815","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49378","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56816","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-49379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56817","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56818","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-49380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56819","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49381","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56820","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-49382","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56821","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-49384","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56822","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-49386","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56823","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-49388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56824","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-49390","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56825","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-56826","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-49393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56827","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56828","text":" "},{"id":"spn-56829","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-56830","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-49394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56831","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49395","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56832","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-49396","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56833","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56834","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-49397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56835","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49398","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56836","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-49399","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56837","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-49402","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56838","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-49403","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56839","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-49405","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49408","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56840","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-49407","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56841","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-49410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56842","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56843","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-49411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56844","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49412","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56845","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-49413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56846","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56847","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-49414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56848","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49415","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56849","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-49416","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56850","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-49418","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56851","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-49420","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56852","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-49422","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56853","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-49424","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56854","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56855","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-49427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56856","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49428","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56857","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-49429","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56858","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56859","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-49430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56860","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49431","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49433","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56861","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-49432","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56862","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-49435","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56863","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id":"blk-49436","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56864","text":"BYOR (Bring Your Own Repo) ingestion — point PRISM at any repo and it will"}]}],"id":"blk-49438","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56865","text":"generate scenarios"}]},{"id":"blk-49441","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56866","text":"IRT calibration of scenario difficulty"}]}],"id":"blk-49442","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56867","text":"Leaderboards, regression detection, fix suggestions"}]}],"id":"blk-49444","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56868","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-aware:"},{"id":"spn-56869","text":" reads any system's PULSE manifest at runtime and injects"}]}],"id":"blk-49446","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56870","text":"scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-56871","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-56872","text":" boundary, observing outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-56873","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-56874","text":" phase"}]},{"id":"blk-49449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56875","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint:"},{"id":"spn-56876","text":" A diagnostic that measures *learning over time* must itself be a closed loop — it must reflect on its own scenarios and evolve them based on what the inner loop fails on. Hence the 4-phase evaluation structure."}]},{"id":"blk-49450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56877","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-56878","text":" "},{"id":"spn-56879","marks":["code"],"text":"/PRISM/"},{"id":"spn-56880","text":" Elixir/OTP codebase, Fly.io, 6 MCP machines ("},{"id":"spn-56881","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-56882","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56883","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-56884","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56885","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-56886","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56887","marks":["code"],"text":"reflect"},{"id":"spn-56888","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56889","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose"},{"id":"spn-56890","text":", "},{"id":"spn-56891","marks":["code"],"text":"config"},{"id":"spn-56892","text":"), "},{"id":"spn-56893","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://prism.opensentience.org"}],"text":"prism.opensentience.org"}]},{"id":"blk-49451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56894","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-49452","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56895","text":"OS-010: PULSE — Protocol for Uniform Loop State Exchange"}]},{"id":"blk-49453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56896","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-56897","text":" Closed-loop control theory (Wiener cybernetics 1948) + temporal cognition (Allen interval algebra 1983)"}]},{"id":"blk-49454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56898","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-49455","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49457","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56899","text":"Loop manifest schema (JSON Schema): "},{"id":"spn-56900","marks":["code"],"